Phase 6 continuation 2026-10-09. Pinned Java checkout remains read-only at commit efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9.
The pinned Java constructor/reflected-proxy oracle now covers 397 `socksConstruction` cases, including every escape follower U+0000–U+00FF and 15 Unicode/control probes. New `\u` probes cover all nibble positions and supplementary scalars that straddle the four-UTF-16-unit boundary. Java accepts `A\u123𝟚Z`, producing UTF-16 units [65,4661,57306,90]; native represents the lone low unit as U+FFFD. Java also accepts `A\uD83𝟚Z`, where the decoded high unit and leftover low unit form U+1D7DA; native preserves that scalar.
The 396-case regression first failed because Rust rejected `\u123𝟚`; oracle/test commit 7cb2552 adds the first four cases. Pairing test commit 4ae4dc9 adds the valid decoded-surrogate pair. Implementation 77f6bd8 consumes the exact UTF-16 unit width, retains any unit crossing the boundary, preserves a completed pair, and replaces only an unpaired unit. Current `client-config.json` SHA-256: 782e9c5ef3c8523d7de1ee0d61c9ad0cf16fc8036e65e6c296a26a1e6df824ab.
Validation passed: `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked --quiet` (local loopback access enabled); `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`; pinned offline Maven verify (22 scenarios); comparator self-test and manifest validation (22 scenarios); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`. The focused 397-case SOCKS differential passes.
Updated ADR-0038 and the Phase 6 API/config, Java compatibility, requirement, and runtime audits. No plan files or pinned Java source checkout were edited; no Broker/Docker was used. This closes only the invoked escape cases. Broader DTO and source/API/input reconciliation remains open; Phase 6 is still partial and P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.
